- op: discuss  # 6a2f
  at: '2026-10-03T06:41:57Z'  # 6a2f
  by: agent  # 6a2f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6a2f
  clock: 6  # 6a2f
  nonce: 6a2f  # 6a2f
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). Premise holds; title, count and mechanism corrected.\n- MECHANISM: the WI-motiz floor (#1390, 79c203145b) assigns a floor id per file ONLY when the floor key is unique and leaves same-name groups NULL (ADR-0035 floor paragraph). Same-file overloads get stable_id=null, not an emission-order ordinal. Seen null: cuda f x2, glsl f x2, julia f(::Int)/f(::String), elixir Demo.greet x3, proto S.Get/T.Get.\n- COUNT: ~31 language families, not ~20. All 22 named still ride the floor. Not named before: capnp method (14 floor / 11 null), tlaplus operator (44/2), proto rpc method (null), commonlisp, fsharp, jupyter functions, dart constructor (dart functions/methods are producer-computed), wgsl function (mixed 3 producer / 3 floor / 2 null), cobol program, fortran program/subroutine. Member kinds still floor: csharp property, swift property, php field, scala object, agda field, zig field.\n- RE-SCOPE PROPOSAL: phoenix/lib re-measured at HEAD = exactly 699 nulls (672 function, 27 macro) of 2,221; the lossy-signature point holds (greet(:a) emits signature \"()\"). Weak spot in step 3: \"floor_abstained = 0 means the floor is exact\" fails as soon as a same-name sibling is added; for overloading languages (cuda, glsl, julia, fortran generics) adding one overload turned 0 into 2 nulls. Acceptance for those needs an add-a-sibling test, not a zero on one sample.\n- Scheme: ADR-0035:167 + owner 10-01: a producer value replacing a floor value is no scheme bump.\n- NOT CHECKED: verilog/systemverilog/vhdl/astro/blade/twig/meson/prisma/sparql callables (fixtures produced none); SQL procedures, Rust/C macros (no symbol emitted).\nTitle updated to match."  # 6a2f
- op: discuss  # af77
  at: '2026-10-12T08:00:20Z'  # af77
  by: agent  # af77
  actor: jgstern_agent  # af77
  clock: 7  # af77
  nonce: af77  # af77
  message: "OWNER SCOPE DECISION 2026-10-12 (relayed by agent): resolve by FINISHING the ADR-0035 migration, not the 2026-10-02 narrow re-scope. (1) Move every producer that still rides the WI-motiz floor (~31 language families incl. member kinds) onto the ADR-0035 producer formula (compute_stable_id / make_typed_stable_id with scope chain + structural inputs), including languages that show 0 floor_abstained on a sample (adding one overload turns 0 into 2 for cuda/glsl/julia/fortran). (2) Shared arity functionality for grammars where compute_stable_id finds no params node (elixir, erlang, haskell, ocaml, clojure, ...), so the discriminant comes from one shared helper, not per-language one-offs. (3) Enforcement: a null stable_id becomes a failure through a per-language shrink-only baseline ratcheted to 0, plus a cross-language delete-an-earlier-sibling test (no other id moves). No new contract or helper design beyond (2). Expected to land as several PRs."  # af77
- op: discuss  # 1a96
  at: '2026-10-12T18:05:13Z'  # 1a96
  by: agent  # 1a96
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1a96
  clock: 8  # 1a96
  nonce: 1a96  # 1a96
  message: "B1 LANDED (PR #1558, merge a496d97379; status unchanged, campaign continues). GATE: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_id_floor_gate.py runs the full pipeline over 79 per-language fixtures, each with an earlier same-name sibling, then with it deleted, and ratchets against shrink-only .ci/stable-id-floor-baseline.json: (1) floor_and_null = per (language, kind) count of callable/member records (function method constructor macro operator procedure subroutine program getter setter multimethod arrow_function property field object subscript) whose stable_id equals the floor key or is null; (2) sibling_deletion_moves = languages where the deletion moved, nulled or dropped another id. Growth AND shrink fail, so every migration PR rewrites its rows. Gate functions live in the test module (WI-ratuv forbids new prod functions with test-only callers); .ci/coverage-only-deps.txt maps all 78 analyzer files + base.py to it. BASELINE: 38 languages, 67 floor + 43 null; 38 languages fail the deletion check, including producer-computed ties (cpp, hlsl, nim, ada, pascal, sql, scheme, racket, bash, v, purescript, solidity) and line-hashed ids (pony, scss, twig) whose fix changes computed values (ADR-0035 §6 call needed). SHARED ARITY: overload_arity.declared_arity(meta) + declared_arity_stable_id(...) (untyped tier = compute_stable_id's value for the same params; typed tier when a parameter declares a type); behaviours.callback_stable_id mints through it byte-identically (pinned). Evidence: pytest packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_stable_id_floor_gate.py on dev a496d97379 -> 14 passed. Analogues: ocaml/agda/lean/wolfram DROP the second same-name callable (filed INV-kagib-tugal-novif-tival-hivun-hurag-vujaf-jazov); grpc-linker nulls are INV-fufij. Per-language inventory (fixture + 25-files/language corpus sample), migration list with sizes and proposed batches B2-B8: LEDGER of the campaign plan, scratchpad fixes/tusad/TUSAD_PLAN.md."  # 1a96
