  message: "B4 LANDED (PR #1562, merge 907d2f25d3; status unchanged). INV-kagib fixed first and set satisfied: ocaml/agda/lean/wolfram no longer drop a second same-name declaration. Migrated to declared_arity_stable_id with scope chains: haskell (function arity from equation patterns, data, instance), ocaml (module chain, local fns f/g), fsharp (module chain, records/unions/fields), elm (params, port), agda (module/data/record/where chain, fields), lean (namespace stack, theorem/inductive/instance), tlaplus (LET-local A/f, constant/theorem/assumption), wolfram (each definition; pattern heads/literals as typed discriminant). Names change for nested scopes (A.run, Pair.fst, A.Point.X, Shape.helper); ocaml local let-values no longer emitted. Producer ids byte-identical before/after on fixtures + corpus sample. Baseline 31 langs 52 floor / 28 null / 32 deletion failures -> 23 langs 34 floor / 24 null / 26. EVIDENCE on dev 907d2f25d3: delete-an-earlier-sibling via hypergumbo run per language -> haskell 3/3, ocaml 3/3, fsharp 3/3, elm 3/3, agda 11/11, lean 2/2, tlaplus 4/4, wolfram 2/2 survivors same id, 0 null. Corpus sample floor/null (all kinds) -> 0 for all seven languages with corpus files (ocaml 991 fn, haskell 555, agda 556, lean 512, tlaplus 155+2 null, elm 147, fsharp 39); no wolfram corpus files. F# class types/members not emitted: filed WI-tamib. For the scheme-bump batch: qualify table-kind names in nested scopes. Ledger: scratchpad fixes/tusad/TUSAD_PLAN.md."  # 6ca3
